Title: make check cannot run in a fresh container: no declared Python dependencies
Created: 2026-08-31
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-08-31T05:38Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

`CLAUDE.md` opens its conventions with "`make check` must be green before any
commit". In a fresh Claude-Code-on-the-web container on 2026-08-30 it could
not run: the gate reached its last step and died on
`No module named pytest`, and installing pytest then exposed
`No module named numpy` from `tests/test_x8_cross_provider_fidelity.py`. Both
were installed by hand and the suite then passed (264 passed, 12 skipped), so
nothing is wrong with the tests — the dependencies are simply undeclared.

The repository has no `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, `setup.py` or
`Pipfile` at root. The Python under `bench/`, `tests/` and
`verification/probes/` imports `numpy`, `pytest`, `sentence_transformers` and
`torch` beyond the standard library, plus `ruff` as the lint gate's binary.
Nothing states which of those a contributor needs for `make check` as opposed
to for running a measurement driver, and that distinction matters: the heavy
two are a driver's dependencies, not the gate's.

Why this is above the tidiness floor. The rule that keeps this repository
honest is that the gate runs before every commit. An agent session that cannot
run the gate either commits without it or, worse, reports the guards green
having silently skipped pytest — the failure is at the end of a long output,
after eight guards have printed success. That is the same shape as the defect
class ticket 0486 names: a declared thing with no consumer, discovered late.

## Actions

1. Declare the gate's dependencies — the set `make check` alone needs, which
   on today's tree is `ruff`, `pytest` and `numpy`.
2. Declare the drivers' dependencies separately, so a documentation reader is
   not told to install `torch` to run a lint gate.
3. Decide the delivery: a dependency file the contributor installs, or a
   `SessionStart` hook that prepares a web session, or both. The hook is what
   makes a remote session green without a human, and it is the only one that
   fixes the case this ticket was found in.
4. Make the gate fail LOUDLY on a missing dependency rather than at the tail
   of a successful-looking run — a preflight that names what is absent.

## Test

- Red first: in a container with neither package, `make check` must report the
  missing dependency by name in its first lines, not its last.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The gate's dependencies declared, separately from the drivers'
- [ ] A fresh container runs `make check` green with no hand-installation
- [ ] A missing dependency is reported before the guards run, not after
